## RULED BY TUESDAY (verbatim; these are rulings, not options)
1. **B534-1 (Major): take the gate's fix-shape.** Key ids by a symmetric form, so that both cases of every letter + mark pair reach the same key. The regression is the gate's: a theory over the six letter + mark pairs plus U+0130 / `i`+U+0307 and U+1E97 / `T`+U+0308, and the case-flip property. This is the product owner's own ruling made true: live board 2026-10-23 13:35, card `mpscalc-source-version-id-twins-1023` = **a**, "Treat them as the same id (refuse the copy)"; option a's text: "Ids are compared ignoring letter case and accent form. A later MPS lane builds it red-first with tests; the refusal uses the existing duplicate-id message, so no new words." The refusal is the existing `DUPLICATE_SOURCE_VERSION_ID`; no new word.
